//! The EVKB's SDRAM setup (MT48LC16M16A2, 32 MiB on SEMC at 0x8000_0000),
//! as DCD commands.
//!
//! The values are those of NXP's MCUXpresso SDK board file
//! `boards/evkbimxrt1050/dcd.c` (repository `nxp-mcuxpresso/mcux-sdk`,
//! generated by the MCUXpresso Config Tools for MIMXRT1052xxxxB,
//! "DCDx V2.0"), unchanged and in the SDK's order: the unit tests compare
//! the encoding byte for byte with that file's `dcd_data[]`
//! (`fixtures/evkbimxrt1050-dcd.bin`, its 1040 bytes). The SEMC writes
//! also agree with the SDK's `evkbimxrt1050_sdram_init.jlinkscript`
//! (which differs only in its final SDRAMCR3 value).
//!
//! The script: open every clock gate; SYS PLL (PLL2) on, its PFD2 at the
//! SDK's setting; SEMC clocked from PLL2 PFD2 / 2 (CBCDR); the GPIO_EMC
//! pads muxed to SEMC (EMC_39, the DQS pad, with SION) with pad setting
//! 0x110F9; the SEMC controller, the SDRAM on CS0 (BR0 0x8000_001B:
//! 0x8000_0000, 32 MiB, valid) and its timings; then the JEDEC power-up:
//! PRECHARGE ALL, AUTO REFRESH twice, MODE SET (0x30), each IP command
//! followed by a wait for SEMC_INTR.IPCMDDONE; finally auto refresh on.
